@COMMENT {

% strings for additional journal titles and conferences
% Author: Ulrich Schuster, Moritz Borgmann

This file contains string definitions for journals and conferences
these strings are not included in the IEEEabrv.bib file, and can be used in addition.

identifiers:
 J  = Journal
 C  = Conference
 CU = Conference (proceedings not yet available) (stands for "conference unpublished")

Usage of conference identifiers
before conference proceedings have appeared, include the following in the BibTeX record,
as an example:

  intype     = "presented at the",
  booktitle  = IEEE_CU_GLOBECOM,

after the proceedings have appeared, add the page numbers and volume, remove the intype
field, and change the "CU" identifier in the conference macro to "C":

  booktitle  = IEEE_C_GLOBECOM,
  volume     = 1,
  pages      = {142--148},

See end of file for rules for abbreviation.

### Cleaned by bibfix normalizer ###
  command: bibclean --noexpandmacros --fixstrings  confs-jrnls.bib
}

